# Phase brief standards

A phase brief is the single source of truth for a build. Briefs are LOCKED before
execution. Halt on drift from the brief; log the drift, do not silently deviate.

## Step 0 (mandatory, before any build step)
Step 0 is sacred. Every probe either confirms or changes the design. It gathers:
- Git state + branch-base sanity off the real deployed tip (branch is currently
  `feat/design-1`, confirm the working tree before branching).
- Read every file before editing. FIND line numbers, never assert them.
- File-path collision check before adding routes/components.
- Live data probes Jake runs and pastes back. NEVER fabricate a CE site fact, a
  Sanity query result, or an image/field figure (see 20-probes).

## Trace every behavior to a named file in a numbered step
Behaviors described but never given a step ship broken ("built != working").
Exit criteria map to real file paths. No orphans. Every template behavior traces
to a component, a GROQ projection, a Zod schema, and a route.

## Structure
ASCII wireframes for major screens. Numbered surgical steps with exact file
paths. Exit-criteria checklist mapped to real paths. Explicit non-goals.
Deferred-items table. Decisions-for-human section (ideally "none expected").
D-prefix identifiers for architectural decisions; DEV-N log for mid-execution
deviations. Commit the brief at authoring time.

## Per-template SEO + GEO contract (every template brief)
SEO is specified IN the brief, never retrofitted. Each template brief states:
- Heading hierarchy (one H1, logical cascade).
- The correct JSON-LD schema.org type (BLOG = BlogPosting + BreadcrumbList +
  FAQPage; others get their right type).
- Meta fields wired from Sanity (title, description, OG, canonical).
- Internal linking / entity cross-links.
- Where the template emits clean entity + answer-shaped data for AI search.
Design and SEO decisions belong in the spec, not bolted on post-template.

## Pre-TEMPLATE prep block (template phases only)
1. Screenshot re-capture pass (8-10 per template incl. hover/interaction/fold).
2. Per-template visual reference doc (screenshots + field-to-UI map + complexity
   rating).
3. Per-template QA thresholds (not global).
4. Storybook stories (optional; prioritise for human-developer handoff).
5. Standardised v0.dev prompt template with new CE design tokens.

## Audit
Self-audit the brief first. For schema-heavy, security-heavy, foundational, or
HIGH-complexity briefs, run a cross-model audit via the `.audit/` kit (see
30-safety and the Cross-Model Audit Kit guide): brief to disk -> run the kit
-> read synthesis.md -> fold findings back. The cross-model pre-build audit
catches what a single-model self-audit misses.

## Post-phase context-file gate (tiered cadence)
- TIER 1, ALWAYS (bundled into phase-close commit): CHANGELOG.md (1 line),
  CLAUDE.md (phase table row + stamp), PHASE_HISTORY.md (3-5 line paragraph).
- TIER 2, WHEN CHANGED: FEATURE_MAP.md, CONVENTIONS.md, REGISTRY.md, SCHEMA.md,
  COMPONENTS.md, CAPABILITY_LOG.md.
- TIER 3, FOUNDATIONAL / HIGH-COMPLEXITY / PRE-LAUNCH ONLY: pre-flight context
  audit, deep cross-file audit, post-phase coverage matrix.
Phase weight: STATIC-1 + HOME = Tier 3. SERVICE + TECHNOLOGY = Tier 3.
SCAFFOLD-AUDIT + QA-1 + LAUNCH = Tier 3. COMPARE + CUSTOMER_STORY = Tier 1 + Tier
2 lookout. Simple pattern-apply (TEAM_MEMBER, REVIEW, VIDEO, DOWNLOAD, TOOL,
EVENT, BOOK_A_CALL) = Tier 1 only.
No silent skips: if a normally-updated file was untouched, say why in one line.
